<h1>Cau Giay by Motorbike: Motorbike Day-Ride Ideas in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Cau Giay is the district where a day ride begins at the end of your street. The boulevards run east through Ba Dinh's monument quarter to the Old Quarter and Hoan Kiem Lake, they run north to West Lake and the Tay Ho cafe belt, and they run west out of the city into the suburbs and the open roads beyond, and every one of them is a day waiting to be ridden. The rental counter at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River, hands over the machine, and from there the district does the rest. This page is a menu of day rides built on landmarks and rider comfort, not on invented schedules, because no honest guide quotes a duration for Hanoi traffic.</p>
<p>We cover what a Cau Giay day ride looks like, the West Lake loop, the eastern ride to Ba Dinh and the Old Quarter, the western day into the suburbs, the river day to Long Bien, folding weather into the plan, choosing the machine for the day, and a flexible week that strings the rides together. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and browse wider riding advice in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>.</p>
